    "summary": "I built a single-cell storage box: one full hex base holding a full-depth bin, closed on top by a solid cover. The lid is held shut by magnets. Magnets come on by default with this cover; when I tried to turn them on, the configurator said nothing would change. The parts list includes 6 Ø5×1 mm neodymium magnets and 6 steel BBs (4.5 mm, copper-coated). I closed the six side faces with solid end caps. The joint-locking step didn't need to add any bolts. That makes 12 printed parts, about 628 g of filament and roughly 848 minutes of printing. The configurator's check found no rule errors and no collisions.",
